hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15690","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb, meaning Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Misri, narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard it from Harun. Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, from Hubayb ibn Mughfil al-Ghifari, that he saw Muhammad al-Qurashi standing dragging his lower garment. So Hubayb looked at him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever treads it arrogantly, treads it in the Fire."
"15691","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, he said: Aslam Abu Imran informed me, from Hubayb al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever treads upon his lower garment arrogantly, treads in the Fire of Hell."
"15692","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam, that he heard Hubayb ibn Mughfil, the Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he saw a man dragging his cloak behind him and treading it. So he said: Glory be to Allah. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever treads it from arrogance, treads it in the Fire."
